CHECK bb26.1 TRUE at n = 21, 57, 201 and 1001 earth stops with code 5 when 1 - RSq falls below 1e-10/(n - 1), up to earth's rounding (every flip lies within 3% of it)
CHECK bb26.2 TRUE the flip moves by less than 1% when y is multiplied by 1e6 or 1e-6, so the rule is relative
CHECK bb26.3 TRUE with thresh = 1e-13 the flip stays at the floor, and with thresh = 1e-12 it moves to 1 - RSq = 1e-12
CHECK bb26.4 TRUE earth reports rss = 0 and rsq = 1 when its RSS is small in absolute terms (here up to 4.83e-11), while the residuals give the true value
CHECK bb26.5 TRUE at n = 3001 earth's decision near the floor is not monotone: over two designs it stops at up to 1.51 times the floor and goes on at down to 0.92 times it, and every decision against the rule lies within 1.7e-14 * TSS of the floor, below 1e-13 * TSS
CHECK bb26.6 TRUE at n = 30001 (design 2) earth does not stop by the floor at 1e-4, 0.01 or 0.5 times it
CHECK bb26.7 TRUE with two responses and y times 1e-3, 1e-2 and 1, earth stops with code 5 exactly when the summed RSS is below a value between 1e-11 and 1e-9 in the units of y, while RSS/TSS at the flip changes by a factor above 1e5: the floor is absolute
CHECK bb26.8 TRUE with two responses and y times 1e-4 earth does not stop at 3 terms at any noise level, and with y times 100 and 1000 stops and go-ons alternate as the noise changes (14 and 21 switches)
CHECK bb26.9 TRUE earth reports gcv 0 and grsq NaN at y times 1e-5, and rss 0 and rsq NaN at y times 1e-6, with gcv.per.subset and then rss.per.subset 0 at every size; the selected terms (8 of 10) are those at y times 1 at every scale down to 1e-8
